- papluca/xlm-roberta-base-language-detection — MIT License
  https://huggingface.co/papluca/xlm-roberta-base-language-detection
- philomath-1209/programming-language-identification — WTFPL
  https://huggingface.co/philomath-1209/programming-language-identification
  NOTE: the WTFPL is extremely permissive — it grants essentially unrestricted
  use — but it is not OSI-approved and some organisations' policies reject it
  outright.

  Be clear about what this means in practice. This artifact is downloaded by
  prewarm.py and baked into every image built from this repository, so the
  image redistributes it regardless of policy configuration. Setting
  `code.enabled: false` stops the `code` detector running; it does NOT remove
  the artifact and is therefore not a licence opt-out.

  An organisation that cannot accept the WTFPL must build an image without it:
  remove CODE from `ALL` in app/model_registry.py and set `code.enabled: false`
  in policy.yaml. The detector is then unavailable and nothing else changes.
